/-!
# Explicit words for the proposed Fi₂₃ stabilizer chain

These 48 straight-line words are elements of the exact lifted subgroup by
construction. GAP supplied candidate generator lists for successive point
stabilizers at labels 508, 509, 510, 511, 512, 518, 538, 1163. This module makes
no assertion that those lists generate the point stabilizers. The only proved
subgroup claims are the initial group, the terminal trivial group, and
containment of every listed group in the lifted subgroup.

The shared intermediate subgroup is `wordStage 4`, generated by words 23, 26,
29, and 32. It permits the first and last four stabilizer reductions to be
certified independently, with a literal common interface. The words use Lean
multiplication; the corresponding GAP words act by the inverse permutations.

Source: ATLAS F24G1-p306936B0 and GLS3 Table 5.3v. The straight-line data and
reproducible transcription are in `source/faithfulness/`; their external
computational provenance does not supply any Lean stabilizer theorem.
-/

